Java Learning Roadmap for Automation Testing


✅ Stage 1: Java Basics
These are foundational concepts every tester needs.

🔹 Java Syntax & Structure

🔹 Data Types & Variables   

🔹 Operators (arithmetic, relational, logical)

🔹 Control Statements:

if, else if, switch

Loops: for, while, do-while

✅ Stage 2: Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
Core for writing structured, reusable automation scripts.

🔹 Classes & Objects

🔹 Constructors

🔹 this keyword

🔹 Inheritance (extends)

🔹 Polymorphism (method overloading & overriding)

🔹 Encapsulation (getters/setters, private fields)

🔹 Abstraction (abstract classes & interfaces)

✅ Stage 3: Methods & Modifiers
Learn how to define and use reusable logic.

🔹 Method declaration and overloading

🔹 Static vs Non-static

🔹 Access Modifiers: public, private, protected, default

🔹 Final keyword

✅ Stage 4: Java Collections & Data Handling
Used heavily in test data management.

🔹 Arrays

🔹 Collections Framework:

ArrayList, LinkedList, HashSet, HashMap

🔹 Iterating collections (for-each loop, Iterator)

🔹 Generics

🔹 Sorting and searching with Collections utility class

✅ Stage 5: Exception Handling
Helps manage script failures gracefully.

🔹 Try-catch-finally blocks

🔹 Multiple catch blocks

🔹 throws and throw keywords

🔹 Custom exceptions

✅ Stage 6: File Handling
Used for reading test data (like Excel, config files).

🔹 Reading and writing files using File, FileReader, BufferedReader, etc.

🔹 Working with Properties files

🔹 Intro to external libraries (e.g., Apache POI – optional later)

✅ Stage 7: Useful Java APIs & Libraries
Common for automation scripting.

🔹 String & StringBuilder

🔹 Math and Random

🔹 Date and Time APIs (Java 8+: LocalDate, LocalTime)

🔹 System class and environment variables

✅ Stage 8: Java 8+ Features (Optional but Useful)
Useful in modern frameworks.

🔹 Lambda expressions

🔹 Streams API

🔹 Functional interfaces

🔹 Method references

✅ Stage 9: Practical Java Setup
🔹 Set up JDK

🔹 Use an IDE (IntelliJ IDEA / Eclipse)

🔹 Write, compile, and run Java programs

🔹 Understand .class and .java files




